From 6723a00ee01713274e20b62ea9ba60054f95b263 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes Fix Package <hermes@local>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:57:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] run: tri-state --semantics, wire --semantics-once, idle
 default for --find

- '--semantics off' now overrides an enabled config (was: off only followed
  the config, so an enabled config still spawned the worker); unset follows
  the config, 'fake' forces the fixture adapter even when the config names
  another kind.
- '--semantics-once' was parsed but never read: without it the runner now
  also audits every audit_period_s (proposal section 8), the flag pins the
  mission-start pass only.
- '--find' with no --mission used to default to goto and die with
  '--mission goto needs --waypoint NAME', so the plan's acceptance command
  could not run. --find now defaults to the benign idle mission 'none'
  (new choice); an explicit --mission or --waypoint still wins, and plain
  runs keep the legacy goto default.

Evidence: ../evidence/fix10-{acceptance,off-override,enabled-default}.txt
